                    "label": {
                        "en": "Description"
                    },
                    "value": {
                        "en": "The fifteenth‑century author Maulana Muhammad ibn Husam al‑Din, known as Ibn Husam, wrote the Khavarannama in emulation of the great poet Firdausi’s national Persian epic, the Shahnama. Ibn Husam, however, centers his stories on the Shi'i imam Ali, son-in-law of the Prophet Muhammad. This folio depicts an imaginary meeting between the poet Firdausi and the author of the Khavarannama, Ibn Husam"
                    }
                },
